{"step_index":69,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:46:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:46:19+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:46:19+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 50 to 75\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n50: value to mean \"the least cardinality\" rather than \"there were none\". -/\n51: def HasWitness (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Prop :=\n52:   ∃ s ∈ (univ : Finset V).powerset, p s\n53: \n54: instance (p : Finset V → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : Decidable (HasWitness p) := by\n55:   unfold HasWitness; infer_instance\n56: \n57: /-- Greatest `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does. -/\n58: def maxUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n59:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).max).getD 0\n60: \n61: /-- Least `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `n` when none does. -/\n62: def minUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n63:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).min).getD n\n64: \n65: /- ── order / size ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n66: \n67: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n68: \n69: def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ := G.edgeFinset.card\n70: \n71: /- ── independence / clique ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n72: \n73: /-- `s` is independent: no two of its vertices are adjacent. -/\n74: def IsIndependentFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n75:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, ¬ G.Adj u w\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":70,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:46:19Z","thinking":"**Evaluating graph definitions**\n\nThe code defines `minUpTo`, `eccentricity`, and `radius` for a simple graph. The `eccentricity` uses `minUpTo` with a bound related to the graph's vertex count.  A potential point to examine is the specific use of  `Fintype.card V` as the upper bound `n` in `minUpTo` when defining eccentricity. This could be crucial to the correctness and efficiency of the radius calculation.\n\n\n**Analyzing graph radius and domination**\n\nSince `HasRadius G` implies all vertices are within a radius equal to the graph's cardinality, the `eccentricity` is the smallest such radius for all vertices, therefore a valid radius. The minimum of `eccentricity` across all vertices defines the `radius G`.\n\nNow, considering `totalDominationNumber`, because `HasTotalDominationNumber G` has a witness, the filter over the powerset is nonempty. This means a total dominating set exists and the minimum size defines the `totalDominationNumber`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"CaseInsensitive":false,"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"run_command","SearchPath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/agy.log","toolAction":"Searching the web","toolSummary":"Grep run_command in agy.log"}}]}
